From 4284370dcf4c80b950fb4bac1889eeafb84aac4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:55:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stale REST/edge-function caching, unify cross-page agent
 status, add capability search, and polish buyer portal visuals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add cache: "no-store" to every plain fetch() in the PostgREST/edge-function
  read helpers (buyer-lookup, buyer-vendor-dna, vendor-lookup, vendor-frontier,
  vendor-knowledge, vendor-dna) — these back tight polling loops, and the
  browser's default HTTP cache could silently serve a stale identical-URL
  response instead of the agent's latest write.
- Add useAgentStatus() + <AgentStatusPill>, wired into PortalShell's header
  via a new headerSlot prop and rendered from buyer/layout.tsx — one
  persistent "needs your input" / "all caught up" indicator visible across
  every buyer page, deep-linking straight to whichever page has the pending
  HITL pause instead of leaving the buyer to hunt for it. Also fixes the
  pre-existing set-state-in-effect lint violation in buyer/layout.tsx by
  reading session values directly in the render body.
- Add capability/industry search to /buyer/vendors, searching each
  recommended vendor's published Solution DNA (capability name, category,
  tags) in addition to name/industry/tagline, with a "Matches: <capability>"
  badge on hits.
- Redesign PageHeader (gradient eyebrow badge, entrance animation) and
  StatCard (staggered entrance, hover lift, icon glow ring) — shared
  primitives so the lift applies everywhere they're used.
- Add a shared <LoadingState> skeleton (stats/cards/lines variants) and swap
  it in on the buyer dashboard and vendors page in place of plain
  "Loading…" text.
